@startuml IFC-035-WhatsApp-Integration-Design
title WhatsApp channel: integration design (IFC-035)\nOne seam, two transports, one raw-body webhook route in the API

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11

legend right
  Decision (IFC-035, 2026-11-22): the API's raw-body webhook route
  REPLACES the earlier idea of a Supabase database webhook.
  Why: a database webhook fires after a row exists, so the provider's body
  would already have been stored (and parsed) before anyone checked who sent it.
  The route verifies the HMAC over the exact bytes first, stores only
  authenticated bodies, and answers the provider's retry rules directly.
  Sources: ADR-089, whatsapp-channel-design.md sections 3, 5, 6;
  Meta webhooks overview (retries up to 7 days); WAHA events docs (HMAC sha512).
end legend

actor "Customer's customer\n(WhatsApp user)" as WU
actor "Customer's team\n(Aurora user)" as AU

cloud "Meta WhatsApp Cloud API\n(transport A, official)" as META
cloud "WhatsApp network" as WA

package "Private network (no public address)" {
  component "WAHA container\nNOWEB, pinned by digest\none session + one session key per tenant\ndashboard and Swagger off" as WAHA
}

package "Aurora API (apps/api)" {
  component "Raw-body route\nPOST /api/webhooks/whatsapp/{transport}/{token}\n1. read exact bytes\n2. find connection by hashed path token\n3. verifyWebhook (fail closed, 401)\n4. archive authenticated body only\n5. parseWebhook -> events\n6. 200 fast" as ROUTE
  component "Ingest use case (IFC-324)\nmatch number -> contact -> lead\nidempotent on provider message id\nignore groups and status/broadcast" as INGEST
  component "Send use case (IFC-327)\nconnection connected\nrecipient is the conversation's contact\nMeta: 24 h window else template\nrestriction and STOP checks" as SEND
  component "tRPC whatsapp.send / thread" as TRPC
  component "Connection settings (IFC-328)\nnotice + acknowledgement\nencrypted secrets" as SETTINGS
  component "WAHA session manager (IFC-330)\nadmin key ONLY here\nmints per-tenant session key + HMAC key" as SESSMGR
}

package "Port and adapters (hexagonal)" {
  interface "WhatsAppTransportPort\nverifyWebhook / parseWebhook\nsend / status (IFC-320)" as PORT
  component "MetaCloudTransport (IFC-325)\nX-Hub-Signature-256 = sha256 HMAC(app secret, raw body)" as ADA
  component "WahaTransport (IFC-326)\nX-Webhook-Hmac = sha512 HMAC(session key, raw body)\nclient bound to ONE tenant's session" as ADB
}

database "Aurora database (RLS per tenant)" as DB {
  [whatsapp_connections]
  [whatsapp_webhook_events (encrypted, 30-day purge)]
  [ChatConversation / ChatMessage]
  [Lead activity: WHATSAPP]
}

' inbound
WU --> WA : message
WA --> META : A: Meta delivers
WA --> WAHA : B: paired phone, WhatsApp Web session
META --> ROUTE : HTTPS POST (retries up to 7 days on non-200;\nduplicates possible)
WAHA --> ROUTE : HTTP POST over private network\n(configurable retries)
ROUTE ..> PORT : verify + parse
PORT <|.. ADA
PORT <|.. ADB
ROUTE --> INGEST : normalised events
INGEST --> DB : store message + lead activity (Received)

' outbound
AU --> TRPC : reply from the lead page
TRPC --> SEND
SEND ..> PORT : send
ADA --> META : Graph API /messages (token)
ADB --> WAHA : /api/sendText (session key)
SEND --> DB : outbound message + activity
META --> ROUTE : status webhooks (sent, delivered, read, failed)
WAHA --> ROUTE : ack webhooks

' admin
AU --> SETTINGS : choose a transport,\ntick the notice (B: against WhatsApp terms)
SETTINGS --> DB
SETTINGS --> SESSMGR : B only
SESSMGR --> WAHA : admin key: create session, mint keys

note bottom of ROUTE
  Bytes, not strings: pass the Buffer to verifyWebhook.
  The Stripe route converts the body with toString('utf8') before use;
  that is fine for Stripe, but an HMAC over a decoded string can differ
  from one over the received bytes if the body is not valid UTF-8.
  Proven live against WAHA 2026.10.1: a body re-serialised (pretty-printed)
  before verifying fails the signature (artifacts/misc/waha-sandbox-proof.json).
end note

note right of WAHA
  Risk: WhatsApp does not allow unofficial clients.
  The number can be restricted or banned, with its chats.
  Customer ticks the notice; policy is reply-only,
  no anti-detection features.
end note

note left of META
  Risk: cost and process, not ban.
  Per-message prices since 1 Jul 2025;
  service replies charged after 1,000 free per number
  per month from 1 Oct 2026. Templates need approval.
end note

@enduml
